magine:

npm ci

takes:
2 minutes

If every tiny source-code change causes:

npm ci

to run again:

Change code
 ↓
Build
 ↓
Install dependencies
 ↓
2 minutes

Developer experience becomes painful.
But if dependencies are cached:

Change code
 ↓
Build
 ↓
Reuse npm dependency layer
 ↓
Copy changed source
 ↓
Done quickly

Much better.


Better Ordering

Instead:
FROM node:22-alpine

WORKDIR /app

COPY package*.json ./

RUN npm ci

COPY . .

CMD ["npm", "start"]

Now:

package.json

package-lock.json
        ↓
npm ci
        ↓
Dependency layer
        ↓
Source code

If source code changes but package files don't:

Dependency layer
       ↓
   CACHE HIT
       ↓
Copy source

So npm install doesn't need to rerun.

🔥 This is one of the most important Dockerfile optimization techniques for Node.js.